@Times Rita

But tiles and shingles are different things.  Tiles are hard and made with clay or the like and heat, while shingles are strips of asphalt, composite materials); there are also less common wood, rubber and slate shingles.  The latter might also be called slate tiles, so there is some overlap. Shingles are soft and flexible; tiles are hard and brittle.

Shingles may technically be a kind of tile, but we would never call them "tiles."

